cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Independent verification of publicly deposited prion-disease datasets (dcj-study)"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23173672
authors:
  - given-names: Arthur
    family-names: Araújo da Silva
    alias: BlackYuriJDU
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Brazil"
version: v1.0.0-preprint-clean
date-released: "2026-10-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BlackYuriJDU/dcj-study"
abstract: "End-to-end independent reanalysis of the largest sCJD GWAS (GCST90001389) from summary statistics: all three published loci replicate; cluster-level fine-mapping with 1000G LD via Ensembl REST; stratified genomic-inflation diagnostics; colocalization of the STX6 signal with brain STX6 expression (posterior 0.98 for a shared causal variant under default coloc priors; corrected in November 2026); reproduction of the published brain-expression DEG count (GSE160208) under a stated filter order; covariate-adjusted reassessment of blood miRNA signature (GSE140069). Statistical core in standard-library Python, tested against coloc, SciPy and statsmodels."
keywords:
  - prion disease
  - Creutzfeldt-Jakob
  - GWAS replication
  - fine-mapping
  - open science
